## 1. What this document answers, and on whose record

The question is **not** "does the mpd repo still mention RTL somewhere" — it is **"does the mpd repo
still carry RTL capability"**, judged against the split's own governance record adopted as the
acceptance contract by t2 (`scope/acceptance.md`, built on silicon `docs/sync-policy.md` §1/§5 and the
mpd-side removal record): "RTL capability" = the `mpd_verif_*` tool surface, the three RTL skill
trees, the `rtl-ip` team-profile data, the HDL language-service assets (Verible / slang-server), the
waveform-read rows, the RTL guides, and the golden Verilog fixtures.

Inputs, in the order the rulings made them binding:

| Input | Task / author | Role in this verdict |
|---|---|---|
| `captain-rulings.md` | captain | **decides every contested path** (R1/R1.1 LSP, R2 docs, R3 cases, R4 partial-copy loss, R5→R5.1–R5.3 hook, R6 fixtures/pack, R7.1–R7.15 incl. R7.12 installer/build family, R7.13 criterion defects, R7.14 the retained gate's channel, R7.15 Guard-1/Guard-2) |
| `review/review.md` | t6 Plan Reviewer (`^verdict: pass`) | adversarial review; its §6 conditions **C1–C11** are **mandatory** for this synthesis (§6.3 maps them). Per C10 + review §8–§9: `review.md` is one document, but §8.6/§9 were written after t6's terminal record and R7.7–R7.10 are the **captain's adjudications over it**, not review-authored rulings |
| `scope/acceptance.md` | t2 Architect | the acceptance contract: buckets B1–B4, criteria C1–C10, verdict rule (§6: C1–C8/C10 hold ⇒ stripped; any failure ⇒ residual; declared-but-absent allow-list item ⇒ **bridge gap**) |
| `repo-scan/findings.md` + `summary.json` + `raw/census.tsv` | t1 Explorer | exhaustive both-axis census: 4537 distinct hit paths, 16 `FULL-STRIP-DEFECT` (F1–F6), plus declared buckets |
| `cross-repo/{parity,bridge,findings}.md` | t3 Researcher | handover parity (73 claimed / 64 landed / 9 missing / 0 mismatch), bridge reachability, F1–F7 |
| `gates/{gates,findings}.md` + `result.json` + `raw/` | t4 (`**` broken-gate discovery) | the standing-gate measurements and the live-subject table |
| `verify/verdict.md`, `verify/false-negative-probes.md`, `raw/` | t5 Reviewer (owner) | independent re-verification (K1–K5, A1–A6, P1–P20), V1–V9 escalations |
| **`verify/addendum-gates-and-criteria.md`** (t5's owner; filed **separately** after t5's terminal record) + **`verify/addendum-manifest.md`** (t13 index: **§2 = claims A1..A22** for the addendum, **§3 = A23..A34** for `review.md` §8/§9, **§4 = byte-identity/hash lineage**) | t5 Reviewer / t13 Architect | **part of this verdict's evidence base**: its own re-runs of all five gates (A1–A6), the two RTL cases' SKIP-and-exit-0 **executed** rather than quoted (A8/A9), the **three criterion defects** (A11–A13), the **installer/build residual family** (A14–A16), probes P14–P20. It is **not** a verdict change and is not presented as one (manifest §1.1/§4: the t5 verdict stands; `verdict.md` + `false-negative-probes.md` are recorded **byte-unchanged**, hashes in §4 of the manifest) |
