## 2. THE ANSWER

> ## **ANSWER: YES-EXCEPT-LISTED-RESIDUALS**

**One line.** The bulk of the RTL surface did leave mpd — all three RTL skill trees, the whole
`mpd-verif-plugin`, the `rtl-ip` profile data and every RTL row in the shrunk bundle are gone and the
vendor fingerprint converged (skills 329 files) — but the strip is **not complete**: live RTL
capability (mounted HDL language-server registrations and an installer that fetches the HDL servers),
stranded RTL content (six RTL guides, four Verilog fixtures, an HDL template, a stale installable
pack), two green-by-vacuity RTL QA cases and two open bridge gaps (the `rtl-ip` carrier hook and the
README pointer note) remain in the tree at the pin.

* **Why not `NO`.** The capability classes the policy names are individually accounted for: C1 and C2
  hold (§3.1), the RTL rows are absent from every preset/patch/manifest (P11/P17), the corpus
  fingerprint converged at 329 files with one re-pin, and the cross-repo handover is 64/73 landed with
  **0 content mismatches** and **0 mpd-side originals still present** (t3). Nothing here says the
  extraction failed; it says the extraction is incomplete.
* **Why not plain `YES`.** C3, C4, C5 (first half), C6 and C8 all fail as measured (§3.1); the HDL
  registrations are not dormant source but the artifact a mounted session runs (§4.1 row X1); and the
  census's own `BRIDGE-BY-DESIGN / ACCEPTABLE` label on those three paths is superseded by R1.1
  (§4.6).
* **The green gates are not evidence for a `YES`.** `verify-vendor`, `verify-rtl-references` and
  `verify-rows-parity` are green **and cannot witness the strip**: per V3/R7.9 — narrowed to the exact
  measurement by R7.14 — the reference gate's failure channel is unreachable **exactly where it
  matters while the sibling is present**: silicon-owned paths that are **MPD-ABSENT** resolve as
  "resolved" (either-root resolution), the `PENDING` list pre-absolves every audited residual family,
  and the standing run treats `considered: 0` as PASS. **With the sibling absent it does fail**
  (`MPD_SILICON_ROOT=/nonexistent node scripts/verify-rtl-references.mjs` → exit 1, 3 unresolved), so
  the surviving fact is narrower than "structurally unreachable" — and R7.14 makes the repair's
  re-pointed gate **strictly stronger** than today: a positive mpd-side invariant, still failing when
  the silicon side is absent, `considered` printed in the standing run, and `considered: 0` read as a
  degraded run rather than a silent pass. No green gate is allowed to upgrade this answer
  (review §6 C6; review **§8.3**, ruling **R7.9**). **The gate regains evidentiary weight only after
  t8 re-points it and t11 re-measures it in that state** — until then its green may be repeated **only
  as a current-health fact**, never as strip coherence.

