**Verdict rule applied.** Any C1–C8 failure is a residual (repair input); a **declared-but-absent**
allow-list item is a **bridge gap** and must be reported separately — never folded into "residual"
(that would claim an over-strip) and never into "pass" (that would hide a broken cross-repo contract).
C6 is therefore in the bridge-gap section of this verdict, and C7's registration clause is marked
superseded rather than passed.

### 3.2 Three contract defects carried, not inherited as passes (R7.13: corrected, not inherited)

1. **C7's row check is vacuous.** `grep -c '^\| rtl-verif ' skills/dsh-qa/SKILL.md` treats `^` as an
   alternation branch and matches **every line** (measured 73 = the file's line count) while the
   strict row form returns **0**. The criterion therefore passes unconditionally and verifies nothing;
   the repair must replace it with a strict row test and say so. This is the same "guard that cannot
   fail" family as R7.9 — **named twice on purpose**, because this instance sits inside the audit's
   **own contract** (`verify/addendum-gates-and-criteria.md` §4, claim A11; R7.13). Precision: the
   finding is about the **shipped escape form**, and must not be widened into "the pattern cannot
   work" — the strict form does work (review §9.3).
2. **C7's case command cannot survive its own sibling criteria**: it requires the two RTL cases to
   exist and SKIP while C1–C5/R3 retire them; it needs re-specification, not a post-repair run
   (claim A12; R7.13 + R7.2 — stays SUPERSEDED, never passed).
3. **C6 is red on both allow-list remnants** (no hook, no pointer note) — see §3.3 and §4.5
   (claim A13; R7.13: reported as bridge gaps until R5.2/R5.3's hook and mount proof exist; never
   reported as passed in this pre-repair baseline).

### 3.3 The two standing gates RED at the pin — stated as a FACT, with qualifiers

**Fact.** At `32ae54dd10db7ea46e1c1263143d56f266fd1f78` two standing gates are **red**: the required
MOUNT/boot gate exits **1** and the Tests gate exits **1**. Both are confirmed by t4, re-measured
independently by t12, and re-run again by t5 — the same two causes, the same counts
(`verify/raw/g5-exits.txt`: `bundle-lifecycle exit=1`, `bun-test-packages exit=1`).

**F1 — `bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/bundle-lifecycle.mjs` → exit 1** (`boot.ok=false`).

* Cause: the roles probe's corpus expectation `bundled.length >= 20`
  (`packages/mpd-qa-roles-probe/src/index.ts:58`, mirrored in the built `dist/index.js:282`) against a
  post-extraction corpus of **19** (`SKILLS=19 BUNDLED=19` → `[roles-probe] FAIL`).
* **Qualifier 1 (R7.6): the red is EXPECTATION DRIFT.** The same boot log is green everywhere else —
  `install ok`, `composed ok`, `http:true`, the `mpd` preset mounted, `ADAPTER_TOOL_CALL=ok`, the
  11-role `ROSTER=…` line, `SKILL_FIXTURE=ok name=svn-master bytes=5210`, `noHomeCopy ok`,
  `layerDurability ok`, `uninstall ok`, residue `[]`. Writing "the MOUNT gate is red" without this
  qualifier misreads as "the mount is broken".
* **Qualifier 2 (R7.6): it was an INCOMPLETE RE-BASELINE in the extraction commit itself.** `12291a7`
  performed the identical `20 → 19` re-baseline in
  `packages/mpd-bootstrap-plugin/test/bootstrap.test.ts` (its message names the RTL move as the
  reason) and **missed** `packages/mpd-qa-roles-probe/src/index.ts:58` — the commit touched zero files
  under `mpd-qa-roles-probe` (t7 re-verified: `git show 12291a7 --name-only | grep -c mpd-qa-roles-probe`
  = 0). The extraction administered the fix class and left one instance behind.
* Revision key: **RED at `32ae54d`; GREEN at `3d99718`** (the pre-extraction worktree, where the probe
  ran `SKILLS=22 BUNDLED=22` / `PASS` / `ok=true`). Fix is a one-line re-baseline in the repair.

**F2 — `bun test packages` → exit 1 (295 pass / 3 fail, `Ran 298 tests across 64 files`).**

* Cause: `packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/self-fix-tests/registry-context-heal.test.mjs` (2 cases) and
  `scope-glob-and-contract.test.mjs` (1 case) build their "pristine upstream" fixture with
  `git show HEAD:…/lib/tools.js` (resp. `quality-gates.js`) and assert it carries **zero** `mpd-delta`
  markers. `d510a16` committed the delta bodies into that file, so the premise is false at HEAD
  (t7 re-verified: `git show HEAD:…/lib/tools.js | grep -c mpd-delta` = **10**).
* **Qualifier (R7.6): F2 is NOT extraction-caused — it is pre-existing since `d510a16`.** Proven by
  **ancestry**: `git merge-base --is-ancestor d510a16 3d99718` → exit 0 (t7 re-ran it), so the
  baseline commit already carries the markers — and by **byte-identity**: `git diff 3d99718 HEAD --
  packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/` = **0 diff lines** (plugin tree and self-fix tests identical;
  t7 re-ran it). It is **not** proven by the `raw/bun-test-baseline-3d99718.log` log, whose two
  artefacts (duplicate suite paths; 6-vs-3 failure counts for byte-identical files) make it unfit as
  proof; that log stays exactly as emitted and must not be cited.
* Revision key: **RED before AND after the extraction** (`3d99718` and `32ae54d`); the `bun test`
  count changed 376→298 only because the removed plugin suite left with the strip.

**Citation discipline (review §6 C7 / C6).** t4 is cited here as **the broken-gate discovery**, never
as "guard coherence" — t4's own reassignment reason states the tree is NOT coherent. t12's closure
counts `verify-vendor`, `verify-rtl-references` and `verify-rows-parity` among "three gates green";
that is carried **per command only** and never as a strip-coherence signal (V3/K5, R7.9).

