## 5. Coverage honesty — what was NOT verified

* **Nothing silicon-side was re-verified beyond t3's read-only parity.** No silicon file was read,
  hashed, booted or edited by t5, by t7, or by the audit at large beyond t3's read-only inspection. C9
  is reported on t3's record; `A3` is `UNVERIFIABLE` within t5's scope; the silicon half of R1.1
  (whether silicon's own copies stay byte-identical) is **not** adjudicated here.
* **The mounting gates were not re-run by t5.** t5's A4 re-measures F1's *substance* (corpus 19 vs
  threshold 20) and says so; a verdict on the boot itself must come from a mounting boot with
  registration instrumentation, never from `--dump-config` (AGENTS.md §4).
* **`bun test` was not re-run by t5.** F2's sentence in §3.3 rests on t4/t12's measurements plus the
  ancestry and byte-identity proofs; t5 declined the re-run and disclosed it (review §4c).
* **The carrier-hook behaviour (C6) has no proof today** because nothing landed: no hook, no pointer
  note. Its proof obligation — a real mounting boot on a scratch `DSH_HOME` showing the `agent-teams`
  row carrying **both** `mpd` and `rtl-ip` under `config.profiles` while `profiles.mpd` still holds the
  full roster, **plus** the absent-silicon `{}` fallback boot — **does not exist yet** (R5.2/R7.1;
  review §6 C4).
* **The ledger completeness equation (C10's second half) was not independently reproduced** by t5; the
  census's row arithmetic is bookkeeping it could not falsify from its scope.
* **Commands t7 did NOT run.** This synthesis ran **read-only** verification only: `git rev-parse`,
  `git branch`, `git status`, `git ls-files`, `git ls-tree`, `git diff`, `git show`, `git merge-base
  --is-ancestor`, `grep`, `sed`, `ls`, `find`. **No gate was executed by t7** — no `verify-vendor`, no
  `bun test packages`, no `bundle-lifecycle`, no `preset-conformance`, no `test:qa`, no installer run,
  no mounting boot. Every gate number in this document is **quoted** from t4/t12/t5 with attribution
  and revision key; nothing here is presented as a t7 measurement.
* **What the green-but-blind gate cannot say.** `verify-rtl-references.mjs` must never be cited as
  proof that the mpd surface is stripped (V3/R7.9; review §8.3). Precisely (R7.14): **with the sibling present** its
  `resolved` bucket holds paths that are **absent from mpd** and its `PENDING` list pre-absolves every
  audited residual family, so a green run is compatible with every residual in §4 being present —
  demonstrated with an unmodified byte-copy of the gate (`raw/demo-blindness-A.log`); **with the
  sibling absent** it exits **1**. The repair's rewrite must therefore be strictly stronger (§6.1
  step 2), not a SKIP-to-green.
* **The addendum's own limits and lineage.** `verify/addendum-gates-and-criteria.md` (claims
  **A1..A22**, indexed in `verify/addendum-manifest.md` **§2**) is t5's owner's work filed
  **separately** from `verdict.md`; it is part of this verdict's evidence base but is **not** a verdict
  change — the t5 verdict stands, and `verdict.md` + `false-negative-probes.md` are recorded
  byte-unchanged (hashes and the falsification check in manifest **§4**). The addendum was corrected
  after indexing (**r1 → r3**; lineage in manifest §4 and `verify/raw/addendum-revision-log.txt`), so
  the manifest's indexed-r1 fingerprint is expected to differ from the current file — that is not an
  alarm. Its C9 line stays `UNVERIFIABLE` on the silicon side, and its C10 "ledger-equation" half is
  bookkeeping it did not independently reproduce — exactly as in §3.1. **Citation loop: CLOSED on both
  sides.** This verdict cites the addendum by path and attribution (and the manifest for the index and
  the review-side claims A23..A34), which satisfies the lead's half of the manifest's pointer item and
  carries the guard-sweep family (manifest §6, now "UPDATED — both addenda are now citable"); the
  captain's half is satisfied too — `captain-rulings.md` **R7.12 (L334–336) names
  `evidence/rtl-extraction-residual/verify/addendum-gates-and-criteria.md` and
  `verify/addendum-manifest.md` §2 by path**, and the t6 addendum is named in R7.15 (L400) as
  `review.md` §8 with the dissent's location. `verify/verdict.md` remains byte-unchanged and predates
  the addendum by contract, so it neither cites it nor needs to: **this verdict is the lead's report**.
  **Section-numbering note:** the manifest was extended after its first filing, so an older pointer
  that calls **§3** the byte-identity record refers to what is now **§4 "Byte-identity and hash
  lineage"**; cite by section name when precision matters.
* **What t7 DID re-measure (read-only, at 07:52Z on the pinned tree — these are the only t7
  measurements in this document).** mpd HEAD = `32ae54dd10db7e…` on `dev` with a clean tracked tree
  (only `??` evidence entries) · silicon HEAD = `bf3dae2530…` with an empty `git status --porcelain` ·
  `git ls-files skills | wc -l` = **329** · all six `docs/rtl-*.md` tracked · all four
  `tests/golden/fixtures/verilog/**` tracked · `templates/rtl-lsp-client.json` present ·
  `grep -rniE 'verible|slang-server' packages/mpd-mcp-lsp/{overlay,dist}` = **12** · both RTL QA cases
  present · `grep -ci silicon README.md` = **0** · `git grep 'rtl-ip.profile.json' -- packages scripts
  presets` = **0** · `find dist/mpd-package ( … )` = **6** FULL-STRIP paths · `git merge-base
  --is-ancestor d510a16 3d99718` → exit **0** · `git diff 3d99718 HEAD --
  packages/mpd-agent-teams-plugin/` = **0** lines · `git show HEAD:…/lib/tools.js | grep -c mpd-delta`
  = **10** · `12291a7` touched **0** files under `mpd-qa-roles-probe` · the `mcp-lsp` row's launch path
  and the `VENDOR_LOCK.json:39-43` `cli.js` sha pin read at the source. Everything else in this
  document is quoted from t1–t6/t9/t12.
* **Audit-time exception:** `repair/prep-note.md` is t8's staged work order and was still being
  extended while this verdict was written (326 → 382 lines). This document therefore cites it as
  context and never as a measurement.

